---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="Output tokens are slow and fill the GPU for seconds, input tokens are fast but can be cached. Open streams follow from the answer length.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Requests per second at the peak <input type="range" min="10" max="2000" step="10" value="300" data-rps /> <b data-rpsval></b></label>
      <label>Input tokens per request <input type="range" min="200" max="8000" step="100" value="2000" data-in /> <b data-inval></b></label>
      <label>Output tokens per request <input type="range" min="50" max="2000" step="50" value="400" data-otok /> <b data-otokval></b></label>
      <label>Share of input tokens served from the prefix cache (%) <input type="range" min="0" max="90" step="5" value="60" data-hit /> <b data-hitval></b></label>
      <label>Target GPU utilisation at the peak (%) <input type="range" min="40" max="90" step="5" value="70" data-util /> <b data-utilval></b></label>
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: one GPU replica prefills about 20,000 new input tokens per second and decodes about 2,500 output tokens per second across its whole batch, and these two kinds of work share the same GPU time. Each stream receives about 40 tokens per second, and a time to first token of 0.5 seconds is added. A GPU costs about $3 per hour. The 40 teams, the mix of models and the extra cost of long contexts are ignored.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const val = (s: string) => Number(q<HTMLInputElement>(s).value);
    const rows = Array.from({ length: 9 }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const rps = val('[data-rps]'); const inTok = val('[data-in]'); const outTok = val('[data-otok]'); const hit = val('[data-hit]') / 100; const util = val('[data-util]') / 100;
      ['rps', 'in', 'otok', 'hit', 'util'].forEach((k) => (q(`[data-${k}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${k}]`))));
      const inRate = rps * inTok; const newIn = inRate * (1 - hit); const outRate = rps * outTok;
      const gpuSeconds = newIn / 20000 + outRate / 2500; // GPU-seconds of work per second
      const gpus = Math.ceil(gpuSeconds / util);
      const gpusNoCache = Math.ceil((inRate / 20000 + outRate / 2500) / util);
      const streamSecs = 0.5 + outTok / 40; const streams = rps * streamSecs;
      const costDay = gpus * 3 * 24; const outPerDay = (outRate * 86400) / 1e6;
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Input tokens per second', fmt(inRate)],
        ['Input tokens per second that need processing', fmt(newIn)],
        ['Output tokens per second', fmt(outRate)],
        ['GPUs needed at the target utilisation', fmt(gpus)],
        ['GPUs needed with no prefix cache', fmt(gpusNoCache)],
        ['Open streams at once (requests per second times stream time)', fmt(streams)],
        ['Gateway bandwidth to callers, in Mbit per second (about 4 bytes per token)', (outRate * 4 * 8 / 1e6).toFixed(1)],
        ['GPU cost per day if the peak lasted all day, in dollars', fmt(costDay)],
        ['GPU cost per million output tokens at that rate, in dollars', (costDay / outPerDay).toFixed(2)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
